    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 55 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the owner-create/update flow while keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**Schema/contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` string properties to the `OwnerFields` schema (they flow into both the request DTO and the response DTO).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list, so an owner is valid with *either* form of address plus city.\n\n**Persistence**\n- `Owner` entity (`model/Owner.java`): added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns with getters/setters.\n- Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to all four schemas (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/postgres`, `db/mysql`). Tests run on hsqldb (`ddl-auto=none`), so the hsqldb change is the load-bearing one.\n\n**Logic**\n- `NormalizeOwnerAddress`: now normalizes whichever address fields are supplied. When a non-blank `addressLine1` is present it normalizes both lines and sets the flat `address` to the composed value (normalized `addressLine1`, plus a single space and normalized `addressLine2` when present); otherwise it falls back to normalizing the flat `address`. Added a shared `compose(line1, line2)` helper.\n- `RequireOwnerFields`: an address is required in *either* form \u2014 the field error is raised only when both `addressLine1` and the flat `address` are blank after normalization.\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT pipeline): applies the same structured-preferred, compose-on-store behavior so updates stay consistent.\n\nThe MapStruct mapper auto-maps the new fields by name (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`), so the response returns `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and the composed `address` \u2014 e.g. `addressLine1: \"10 king st\"` round-trips as `10 KING STREET` for both `$.addressLine1` and `$.address`, exactly as the new `Cp44`/`Cp12`/`Cp01` tests expect.",
